    "field": "Biogeoscience",
    "problem": "The strong coupling between soil moisture and vapor pressure deficit makes it difficult to disentangle their individual effects on ecosystem production, hindering the ability of models to accurately predict vegetation responses to dryness stress.",
    "method": "The authors propose a method that bins satellite-derived data into percentile-based bins of soil moisture and vapor pressure deficit, which decouples their statistical relationship and allows for the quantification of their individual effects on ecosystem production as measured by solar-induced fluorescence.",
    "task": "The task is to disentangle the coupled effects of soil moisture and vapor pressure deficit on global ecosystem production to determine which is the dominant driver of dryness stress, using satellite observations of solar-induced fluorescence and climate data.",
